## Findings and limits

Blocking found at fixed9c and fixed by652347c: tools/tests/doc/annotated_pages.rs:247 still included the deleted doc/migration/authored/01-architecture.nepld. `cargo test --locked -p nepl3-tools --test doc annotated_pages:: --no-run` exited101 with a concrete missing-file compiler error. The canonical/tests.rs dynamic source selection already followed the registry; this separate typed PageSet fixture was missed. Original failure command/stdout/stderr are retained as old-include.*. Independently checked652347c replaces only that include path with doc/spec/01-architecture.nepld, preserving the complete remaining test bytes. The same no-run command now passes, followed by all five actual annotated_pages tests passing (81 filtered,5.12 seconds). Doc sources, registry, aliases, Markdown and runtime are byte-identical to9c, so the independent generation evidence remains bound to exactly the same production inputs. The final fixture delta and commands are separately retained; no rewrite of the failed9c evidence was made.

Carson's saved GitHub collision evidence was inspected directly and every payload verified. At64deb4 the explicit bootstrap name and GitHub-generated permalink id refer to neighboring positions of the same heading, causing two targets. Its earlier recommendation assuming legacy aliases in both HTML and Markdown was based on an incorrect host-boundary assumption. Direct canonical::html code and actual generated HTML show it never supplies alias JSON: HTML semantic IDs and GitHub legacy aliases must remain separate claims. The title clarification is semantically supported, but actual new GitHub automatic-ID uniqueness/navigation is a different browser review; it is not inferred from this code/generation check. No independent browser, accessibility, file:// bootstrap, deployment, global migration completion or human acceptance is claimed here.

Three Python expectation errors were corrected only in the reviewer helper and preserved: raw Markdown destination spelling was guessed instead of parsing its escaped angle destination; all HTML name attributes were initially counted instead of anchor names; lexical pre framing was initially counted with code payload. Final checks use the actual Markdown parser and nested code text, without changing production or relaxing the expected link/code values. No original source, historical failure or prior review payload was overwritten.
